{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790960696,"nonce":"T0sejqYS/U4UKZuacn4gLKilXNg=","title":"no ash_host_watch, which hlwgpu's browser build imports","message":"xgpu's browser backend settles a request's future on the program's thread when the agent bumps a word: it calls `host::watch(word, handler, context)` before `host::agent` (xgpu-backend template/web.rs). hlwgpu maps that to the import `ash_host_watch` (crates/hlwgpu/src/xgpu/runtime.rs), and xgpu.wasm imports it, but no Ash host defines it; only `ash_host_agent` exists. Host ABI says unknown `ash_host_` imports are refused at instantiation, so the GPU side module cannot load in a page.\n\nWhat it needs: watch a 32-bit word in shared memory; when it changes, run `handler(context)` on the program's thread; return the address of the word the agent adds one to and notifies (the mailbox's `wake`).","files":null}]}